\subsection{A fresh paired test of evaluator size}
We used the repository's fixed 20-puzzle validation pilot drawn from the same 200 puzzles, not a new held-out set. At each root we checked move legality, collapsed equivalent remaining triples, then chose four by a fixed hash order without votes or solvability labels. Local Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and 32B-Instruct scored the same four choices using next-token logits for the answer letters. We ran both the prespecified order and its reversal, yielding [[prompts]] fresh model--prompt evaluations in total. Only after scoring did we label which triples could still reach 24. [[eligible]] of the 20 pools contained such a choice; choosing one of the four uniformly would hit [[chance]] puzzles in expectation.

